<title>USA: Calif. Gov. appoints deputy secretary of rail.</title>
<headline>Calif. Gov. appoints deputy secretary of rail.</headline>
<dateline>SACRAMENTO, Calif. 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>California Gov. Pete Wilson on Friday said he appointed Kenneth Bosanko as deputy secretary for rail and transit at the state Business, Transportation and Housing Agency.</p>
<p>Bosanko, 66, has been the managing director of strategic planning for Southern Pacific Transportation Co since 1992.</p>
<p>He will receive a salary of $82,164 per year. The appointment does not require Senate confirmation.</p>
